   "text": "MP1\nCIRCUIT: Ammeter and variable resistor both shown in series with test wire and with correct symbols.\nMP2\nMETHOD MARK 1: Adjust current / variable resistor until wire melts / current stops. Take current reading.\nMP3\nTHE CHOSEN VARIABLE: metal used or diameter\nMP4\nMETHOD MARK 2: Repeat with other metal(s) or other diameter(s)\nMP5\nVARIABLE TO KEEP CONSTANT: Diameter of wire or metal used, provided it is not the variable chosen for MP3\nMP6\nTABLE with clear columns for current with unit A and for their chosen variable, with correct unit if appropriate.\nMP7\nCONCLUSION: Plot graph of current against diameter\nOR bar chart of current against metal\nOR compare the readings to see if the chosen variable affects the current at which the fuse wire melts",
